---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "How do I apply for a Solihull private hire licence?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Solihull is appointment-only. You must complete the pre-application steps first — Blue Lamp Trust driving assessment, enhanced DBS, Group 2 medical, and the training course and knowledge test — then email licensing@solihull.gov.uk with your full name, date of birth, mobile number and the reason for the appointment. Walk-ins are not accepted.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What DBS check do I need for a Solihull taxi licence?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "An enhanced DBS disclosure — basic and standard are not accepted. It must be for the occupation of taxi/private hire driver under 'other workforce' and include a check of both the adults' and children's barred lists. Solihull uses TaxiPlus, and you must subscribe to the DBS update service within 30 days of the certificate being issued.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What medical do I need for a Solihull PHV licence?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "You must meet DVLA Group 2 medical standards, assessed by a GMC registered medical practitioner on the council's own medical assessment form. The certificate should be dated within 1 month of when you make your application.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What is the Blue Lamp Trust assessment?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "It is the practical driving assessment Solihull requires before you apply, delivered by Blue Lamp Trust. Your certificate needs to be less than 12 months old when you apply for your licence.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "Do I need an HMRC tax check to apply in Solihull?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Only if you currently hold a private hire or hackney carriage licence, or have held one within the last 12 months. Tax check codes expire after 120 days. If you have never held one, you sign a declaration confirming that instead.",
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Apply for a Solihull PHV Licence"
  description="How to apply for a Solihull private hire licence: the Blue Lamp Trust assessment, enhanced DBS, Group 2 medical, training course, knowledge test and booking."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <main class="md:flex md:justify-center">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-[750px]">
      <h1>How to Apply for a Solihull PHV Licence</h1>

      <p>
        This guide explains <strong>how to apply for a Solihull private hire
        licence</strong> (or hackney carriage driver licence) with Solihull
        Metropolitan Borough Council, step by step and in the order you'll
        actually do it. Solihull front-loads the process: almost everything
        has to be finished <em>before</em> you book your appointment.
      </p>

      <p>
        Every requirement below comes from the council's published driver
        licence guide, linked at the bottom of this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Before you book: the pre-application steps</h2>

      <h3>1. Practical driving assessment (Blue Lamp Trust)</h3>

      <p>
        You need a practical driving assessment delivered by
        <strong>Blue Lamp Trust</strong>. Your certificate needs to be
        <strong>less than 12 months old</strong> when you apply for your
        licence, so don't take it too far in advance of the rest.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Enhanced DBS disclosure</h3>

      <p>Your criminal record check must be:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enhanced</strong> — the council will not accept basic or
          standard.
        </li>
        <li>
          For the occupation of <strong>taxi/private hire driver under "other
          workforce"</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Inclusive of a check of <strong>both the adults' and children's
          barred lists</strong>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Solihull uses <strong>TaxiPlus</strong> for these checks, and you must
        <strong>subscribe to the DBS update service within 30 days</strong> of
        the certificate being issued.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Medical assessment</h3>

      <p>
        You must meet <strong>DVLA Group 2 medical standards</strong> — the
        higher standard that applies to professional drivers. The assessment
        must be completed by a <strong>GMC registered medical
        practitioner</strong> on the council's own medical assessment form,
        and the certificate should be <strong>dated within 1 month</strong> of
        when you make your application.
      </p>

      <h3>4. Training course and knowledge test</h3>

      <p>
        The course runs for approximately <strong>4 hours</strong> (breaks
        provided), plus an extra <strong>60 minutes</strong> for the test, and
        is booked through the council's online booking portal. It covers
        safeguarding and CSAE risks including county lines, disability
        awareness and the Equality Act 2010, customer service and
        communication, the Highway Code and road safety, vehicle maintenance,
        and compliance with legislation, conditions and policy.
      </p>

      <p>
        The test itself is <strong>48 questions — 8 on each subject</strong> —
        and you need <strong>36 right (75%)</strong> to pass. Results come
        <strong>within 5 working days</strong>, and the certificate needs to be
        less than 12 months old when you apply. Our
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/solihull/how-to-pass/"
          >guide to passing the Solihull PHV test</a
        >
        covers the format and revision in detail.
      </p>

      <p>
        You can practise for it in the <strong>PHV Prep UK</strong> app, which
        builds mock papers to the Solihull shape — 48 questions, 8 per subject,
        marked at 36/48. It's on
        <a
          href="https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/phv-prep-uk-taxi-badge-test/id6776364932"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">the App Store</a
        >
        and
        <a
          href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.phvprepuk.app&pcampaignid=web_share"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">Google Play</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h3>5. DVLA licence check code</h3>

      <p>
        You need a <strong>check code from the DVLA</strong> so the council can
        view your driving licence record. These codes are
        <strong>only valid for 21 days</strong>, so generate yours close to
        your appointment rather than early.
      </p>

      <h3>6. HMRC tax check (where applicable)</h3>

      <p>
        If you currently hold a private hire or hackney carriage licence, or
        have held one <strong>within the last 12 months</strong>, you need an
        HMRC tax check code. These <strong>expire after 120 days</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you do not hold one and have not held one in the last 12 months, you
        instead sign a declaration confirming that.
      </p>

      <h2>What documents do I need?</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Your <strong>DVLA photocard</strong> (both sides), or both sides of
          the old-style paper licence.
        </li>
        <li>
          A clear, current <strong>passport-style photograph</strong> of your
          head and shoulders.
        </li>
        <li>A <strong>completed application form</strong>.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Proof of your right to work in the UK.</strong> If you have a
          UK passport — current or expired — you must provide it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Bring your Blue Lamp Trust certificate, DBS, medical certificate and
        knowledge test certificate as well, and check the dating rules above:
        several of them expire.
      </p>

      <h2>How do I book my appointment?</h2>

      <p>
        Solihull is <strong>appointment-only — walk-ins are not
        accepted</strong>. Email
        <a href="mailto:licensing@solihull.gov.uk">licensing@solihull.gov.uk</a>
        to book, including:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Your full name</li>
        <li>Your date of birth</li>
        <li>Your mobile number</li>
        <li>The reason for the appointment</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How much does it cost?</h2>

      <p>
        Solihull does not publish its licence, course or retake fees on the
        taxi licensing pages linked below, so we won't quote a figure. Ask the
        licensing team for the current fees before you budget — and remember
        the DBS, medical and driving assessment are separate costs paid to
        their providers, not to the council.
      </p>

      <h2>Where to go next</h2>

      <p>
        The paperwork is the easy part — the test is the hurdle. See
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/solihull/how-to-pass/"
          >how to pass the Solihull PHV test</a
        >
        and the
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/solihull/faqs/"
          >Solihull PHV test FAQs</a
        >. Applying in Wolverhampton instead? We have a
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/how-to-apply/"
          >separate guide for the Wolverhampton process</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Official sources</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.solihull.gov.uk/business/licences/taxi-licensing"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">Solihull Council — Taxi licensing</a
